fact WorkItem(id: "WI-060", description: some(value: "Convert eval to true continuation-passing so deep recursion hits EvalError::DepthExceeded instead of native SIGABRT. Proposal 026 §Activation stack mandates 'no native recursion', but today eval_nested / enter_operation / apply_closure each call run_until recursively — so the Rust call stack grows in lockstep with the activation stack and overflows first. Fix: expand Continuation enum to cover every mid-state (ApplyArg { buffered, remaining }, ApplyArgsComplete { target }, LetBind, MatchScrutinee, IfCond, ClosureResult, …). reduce_* pushes a child frame and returns StepOutcome::Continue; the outer run() loop delivers child results to the parent's Continuation. Prerequisite for honest DepthExceeded semantics and for future Suspension/Branch (VM-style resumption needs a saveable stack). Test: a zero-arg infinite recursion should return DepthExceeded at the configured cap, not SIGABRT."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-044"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Verified(at: "2026-04-19T19:40:08Z"))
